2.2. Data Description
2.2.1 Data Collection
The first step in establishing a good indicator system is to collect enough data. In the process of finding data, we first used the website of the World Bank, and found the corresponding data of the three indicators of threatened birds, namely, the number of bird species, population, forest area, per capita power consumption, and per capita GDP, which are threatened by the impact of light pollution. After continuing to search for other indicator data, we chose the Lancaster University Library for data screening, and successfully found out the lighting market revenue, that is, the sales of lamps and other lighting tools, the temperature anomaly, that is, the number of times that the temperature was considered to be higher or lower than the previous temperature, the proportion of anxiety or depression, and the global proportion of the sales of sleeping pills in various countries, The number of high-rise buildings in each country. Finally, we use the light pollution map tool to find out the brightness, light range, altitude and distance from the sea of the corresponding area.
