2.3.1. Weighted model based on Entropy Weight Method (EWM)
Here we all understand that AHP is associated with subjectivity because of the score matrix. In order to reduce the influence of this property, we use the entropy weight method (EWM) to help calculate the weight. EWM is a method to determine quantitative weights based on the variability of indicators. Generally speaking, the smaller the information entropy of the index, the greater the degree of change of the index value. The more weight it provides. Conversely, the greater the information entropy of the index, the smaller the change degree of the index value, the less information provided, and the smaller its weight. The specific algorithm flow is shown in the figure below.
