3. Metric of light pollution
After selecting indicators and calculating appropriate weights, we need to set appropriate criteria for light pollution levels. In this section, we use the k-means algorithm to establish a suitable standard. According to the K-means algorithm, we get the relevant criteria. According to the collected data, we first cluster each indicator and calculate 3 clustering centers. Then, taking the mean value of index center as the standard boundary, the light pollution degree was divided into normal, good and excellent. The pseudo-code of clustering is shown below:
