4. Conclusion
To sum up, we first established a light pollution risk assessment system to characterize the light pollution risk level of a region. After consulting the data, we should use the combination of AHP and entropy weight method to determine the weight of each index, and make a sensitivity analysis. After that, we use the k-means clustering method to determine the three light pollution levels of excellent, good and normal. Finally, we multiply the weight with the data to obtain the light pollution risk index, and determine the light pollution risk level of a region according to the size of the index. The higher the index, the more serious the light pollution. In addition, reducing light intensity can be a good way to reduce light pollution.


